/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (A nationwide car rental agency needs a database to manage its fleet and customer rentals. Each agency has a unique identifier, a name, and an address. Cars, identified by a VIN, are assigned to an "origin" agency. Customers, with a unique driver's license number, provide their name, phone number, and email. Each rental records the start date, expected return date, total cost, fuel quantity, and any potential damage. Each transaction is managed by an employee with a unique ID and a job title.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
